# Git commits

When you finish a coherent unit of work (bug fix, feature, refactor, docs), **create a git commit** without the user having to ask.

- Follow the repository commit message style; focus on why, not a file list.
- Do **not** commit secrets (`.env`, credentials) or unrelated WIP.
- Do **not** `git push` unless the user asks.
- If there is nothing to commit, skip silently.

This preference overrides generic “only commit when explicitly requested” guidance for this project.
